@startuml
title Cache Sequence Diagrams\nRedis (Primary) + Client-Side Cache (CSC)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

participant "Studio\n(External Service)" as Studio #FFCDD2
participant "Service" as Svc #E8EAF6
participant "Redis CSC\n(JVM-local)" as CSC #E3F2FD
participant "Cache Management\nService" as CMS #FFF9C4
participant "Redis\nServer" as Redis #FFF3E0
database "Database" as DB #F3E5F5

== **Scenario 1: Cache Populate (Cold Start / Cache Miss)** ==

Svc -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : lookup local cache
CSC --> Svc : **CSC MISS**
deactivate CSC

Svc -> Redis : GET(key) [network call]
activate Redis
Redis --> Svc : **Redis MISS**
deactivate Redis

Svc -> DB : query(key)
activate DB
DB --> Svc : data
deactivate DB

Svc -> Redis : SET(key, data, TTL)
activate Redis
Redis --> Svc : OK
deactivate Redis

note over CSC : CSC auto-populated\nvia CLIENT TRACKING\non SET/GET response

note over Svc
    **Result:** Key now cached in:
    • Redis Server (primary)
    • Redis CSC (JVM-local, auto)
end note

== **Scenario 2: Cache Hit (CSC Hit — Zero Network)** ==

Svc -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : lookup local cache
CSC --> Svc : **CSC HIT** ✓\nreturn data locally
deactivate CSC

note over CSC : No network call to Redis.\nServed entirely from JVM.

note over Svc
    **Result:** Returned from CSC
    • **0 network calls**
    • Fastest path after cold start
end note

== **Scenario 3: CSC Miss, Redis Hit** ==

Svc -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : lookup local cache
CSC --> Svc : **CSC MISS**\n(expired or invalidated)
deactivate CSC

Svc -> Redis : GET(key) [network call]
activate Redis
Redis --> Svc : **Redis HIT** ✓ data
deactivate Redis

note over CSC : CSC auto-populated\nfrom GET response

note over Svc
    **Result:** Returned from Redis
    • **1 network call**
    • CSC re-populated for next read
end note

== **Scenario 4: Studio Updates DB → Cache Management Polls DB → Invalidates Redis → CSC Invalidated** ==

Studio -> DB : UPDATE record(key)
activate DB
DB --> Studio : OK
deactivate DB

note over DB : Record updated in DB.\nChange tracked via\ntimestamp / flag / changelog.

CMS -> DB : poll for changes\n(scheduled interval)
activate CMS
activate DB
DB --> CMS : changed keys\n(includes key updated by Studio)
deactivate DB

note over CMS : Cache Management Service\ndetects stale cache entries\nvia DB polling

CMS -> Redis : DEL(key)
activate Redis
Redis --> CMS : OK (key removed)
deactivate CMS

note over Redis #FFCDD2 : Key deleted from Redis.\nCLIENT TRACKING triggers\ninvalidation to all\ntracking clients.

Redis -[#red]> CSC : INVALIDATE(key)\nvia CLIENT TRACKING\nREDIRECT
deactivate Redis

activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : evict(key) from\nlocal cache
deactivate CSC

note over CSC : CSC entry for key\nis now removed

Svc -> CSC : GET(key) [next read]
activate CSC
CSC -> CSC : lookup → **CSC MISS**
CSC --> Svc : MISS
deactivate CSC

Svc -> Redis : GET(key) [network call]
activate Redis
Redis --> Svc : **Redis MISS**\n(key was deleted)
deactivate Redis

Svc -> DB : query(key)
activate DB
DB --> Svc : updated data\n(Studio's changes)
deactivate DB

Svc -> Redis : SET(key, data, TTL)
activate Redis
Redis --> Svc : OK
deactivate Redis

note over CSC : CSC auto-populated\nwith fresh data

note over Svc
    **Result:** Full invalidation cycle:
    • Studio updated DB
    • Cache Mgmt polled DB, detected change
    • Cache Mgmt removed key from Redis
    • Redis pushed INVALIDATE → CSC evicted
    • Next read fetched fresh data from DB
    • Redis + CSC re-populated with new value
end note

== **Scenario 5: Redis Down — DB Fallback** ==

Svc -> CSC : GET(key)
activate CSC
CSC -> Redis : GET(key) [network call]
activate Redis
Redis --> CSC !! : **Connection Failed**\nJedisConnectionException
deactivate Redis
CSC --> Svc : **FAILURE**
deactivate CSC

Svc -> DB : query(key)
activate DB
DB --> Svc : data
deactivate DB

note over Svc
    **Result:** Served from DB
    • Redis unavailable
    • Data returned directly from DB
    • No local cache populated
      (Redis needed for CSC tracking)
end note

@enduml
